MANIFEST

# Virtual environments
.env
# Every .env variant, not just the canonical name. A working copy of this
# repo accumulates `.env.<something>.bak` files during migrations and
# experiments, and they carry the same live credentials the real one does —
# one such backup here held 20 lines of API keys and database passwords.
# `.env` alone does not match them, so a single `git add -A` would have
# pushed those secrets to the remote.
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/

# Database dumps. Same reasoning as .env above: a pg_dump of this system
# carries real case records, user accounts and message history, and must
# never enter git history — including on a private branch, since history is
# not retroactively scrubbable once pushed.
*.dump
*.dump.gz
*.backup
env.bak/
venv.bak/

